# Flagship clip — a live Claude Code session that uses the gadak skill to
# retint an open tab and author a chart dashboard (VHS left | serve tab right).
#
# Regenerated by `bash e2e/demo/record-claude-drive.sh`, which requires:
#   bash tools/tapes/prepare-claude-drive.sh   (frozen demo home + skill install)
#   vhs, ffmpeg, a Claude Code login
# Run `bash tools/tapes/prepare-claude-drive.sh --clean` afterwards — the
# isolated HOME holds a 0600 copy of this machine's credentials.
#
# Nothing here is scripted output: Claude's commands and the HTML it writes
# are the model's. Takes vary; the orchestrator re-runs up to 4 times until
# the result contract holds (two colour changes + a chart dashboard opened).
# Everything visible comes from examples/demo.db. The capture home is frozen.
#
# Left pane is 720×688 so the hstack with the 1160×688 serve tab matches
# FLAGSHIP_L_* in promo-split.ts (tokens/dashboards stay 720×640 | 1024×640).
# No WindowBar: the paper chrome bar is taken from the Playwright half at
# composite time. Font 14 so ~80 columns still fit at 720 px (mcp.tape is
# 20/1080). Vertical (record-claude-drive.sh vertical) rewrites Width/
# Height/FontSize/Padding/Output to 1080×520 @ 18 px — do not put those
# numbers here; this file stays the landscape original. Prompt text is
# not substituted.
#
# Theme: gadak-paper, same identity as mcp.tape / agent.tape.
#
# Size: this tape only records the terminal half. The README gif/mp4 is the
# hstack from e2e/demo/export-claude-drive.sh. Not in `make media` — same
# reason as media-mcp (live Claude Code login + model quota).

Output e2e/.tmp/claude-drive/term.mp4

Require claude

Set Shell "bash"
Set FontSize 14
Set FontFamily "D2Coding, Menlo, Monaco, monospace"
Set Width 720
Set Height 688
Set Theme {"name":"gadak-paper","background":"#f4efe4","foreground":"#1c1812","cursor":"#2e4560","selection_background":"#d5dde8","black":"#1c1812","red":"#8f3530","green":"#2f5e42","yellow":"#8a6418","blue":"#2f5d8c","magenta":"#2e4560","cyan":"#2a4159","white":"#e4d9c4","brightBlack":"#635a4f","brightRed":"#8f3530","brightGreen":"#2f5e42","brightYellow":"#8a6418","brightBlue":"#2e4560","brightMagenta":"#2e4560","brightCyan":"#2a4159","brightWhite":"#f4efe4"}
Set Padding 14
Set Framerate 8
Set TypingSpeed 45ms
Set WaitTimeout 420s

# Neutral shell: no user@host, no real $HOME path. HOME is the throwaway
# agent home, GADAK_HOME is the frozen capture workspace the serve tab uses.
Hide
Set TypingSpeed 1ms
Type "source tools/tapes/.tmp/env-claude-drive.sh || exit 1"
Enter
Type "python3 /private/tmp/gadak-claude-drive/strip-oauth.py"
Enter
Type "python3 /private/tmp/gadak-claude-drive/mark-epoch.py"
Enter
Type "clear"
Enter
Set TypingSpeed 45ms
Show

Sleep 500ms

Type "claude"
Enter
# TUI boot. Take 1 slept 5s and still landed on a bypass-permissions dialog
# (settings now use defaultMode=default + an allow list, matching mcp.tape).
Sleep 7s

# User prompt (English, README audience). One paragraph, two jobs: team look
# then a triage wall with a chart. Claude's command wording is not scripted.
Type "Give this workspace our team's look: purple accent, green quick-win labels, orange bug chips. Then build a triage dashboard — status count cards plus a monthly-opened line chart — and open it."
Sleep 600ms
Enter

# Live model. 300s covers a typical sonnet colour+HTML+save+open pass plus
# a short hold on the opened wall. Idle tail is cut in export-claude-drive.sh.
# Do not Ctrl+C (that prints a resume UUID — mcp.tape).
Sleep 300s
